{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791294019,"nonce":"lGLoQesWauKCE0a0KKUfIu/F2cE=","title":"Cached Xml.parse returns an empty document after the entry changes","message":"Reproducer:\n\n```haxe\nclass CachedXmlParsing {\n    static function main() {\n        var parsed = Xml.parse(\"\u003c!-- child --\u003e\");\n        var manual = Xml.createDocument();\n        manual.addChild(Xml.createComment(\"child\"));\n        Sys.println(\"parsed=\" + Lambda.count(parsed));\n        Sys.println(\"manual=\" + Lambda.count(manual));\n        if (Lambda.count(parsed) != 1) throw \"cached XML parsing\";\n        Sys.println(\"CONFORMANCE_OK\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\nRun twice with the same import cache, changing only entry whitespace between runs to invalidate the full-program MIR cache:\n\n```sh\nRAYZOR_STD_PATH=\"$PWD/compiler/haxe-std\" target/release/rayzor run /tmp/CachedXmlParsing.hx --release --cache-dir /tmp/rayzor-cached-xml-v9\nprintf \"\\n\" \u003e\u003e /tmp/CachedXmlParsing.hx\nRAYZOR_STD_PATH=\"$PWD/compiler/haxe-std\" target/release/rayzor run /tmp/CachedXmlParsing.hx --release --cache-dir /tmp/rayzor-cached-xml-v9\n```\n\nCold: parsed=1, manual=1, CONFORMANCE_OK. After changing the entry: parsed=0, manual=1, uncaught cached XML parsing. Logs: /tmp/rayzor-cached-xml-cold.log and /tmp/rayzor-cached-xml-imports.log.\n\nThe manual-document result establishes that Xml class identity and Lambda.count iteration wrapping work with restored imports. The remaining failure is on the cached XML parsing path. Cache metadata includes Lambda.count's inferred Int return, and the caller now uses a direct integer comparison; this is separate from treating the count as Dynamic. The packaged entry regression and all scored conformance rows run with --no-cache.","files":null}]}